# idle-ping.env — configuration template
# How to use:
#   1. Copy this file to `idle-ping.env` (same folder as the scripts):
#        cp idle-ping.env.example idle-ping.env
#   2. Uncomment the lines you want to change and edit the values.
#   3. Save. Changes take effect within ~1 minute (the gate reads this file
#      on every run) — no restart needed.
#
# Precedence: environment variables > idle-ping.env > built-in defaults.
# You can also skip the file entirely and `export` these as env vars.

# ===== Paths (core) =====
# OpenClaw workspace path (parent of scripts/; auto-detected if unset)
# IDLE_PING_WS=/home/you/.openclaw/workspace

# Path to sessions.json (OpenClaw internal session data; default is fine)
# IDLE_PING_SESSIONS_JSON=$HOME/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/sessions.json

# Cron job IDs of the send / pause jobs (filled automatically by install.sh;
# find them yourself with `openclaw cron list` if needed)
# IDLE_PING_SEND_JOB_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# IDLE_PING_PAUSE_JOB_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Custom system log path (optional)
# IDLE_PING_LOG=$HOME/.openclaw/workspace/curiosity/system-activity.log

# ===== Dice rhythm =====
# Dice denominator — chance to ship per roll is 1/N.
# Default 30 = ~3.3% per roll. Lower = more chatty, higher = more shy.
# IDLE_PING_DICE_RANGE=30

# How often the gate cron job rolls the dice (cron interval, e.g. 1m, 5m).
# NOTE: this only applies when install.sh runs (it sets the cron schedule);
# change it in idle-ping.env then re-run `bash install.sh` to update.
# IDLE_PING_ROLL_EVERY=1m

# Minutes of silence before dice-rolling starts (default 30)
# IDLE_PING_IDLE_MIN=30

# Cooldown after a shipment — no new trigger for N minutes (default 30)
# IDLE_PING_COOLDOWN_MIN=30

# Max shipments per day (0 = unlimited; default 0)
# IDLE_PING_DAILY_CAP=0

# ===== Silent window =====
# Silent window start hour, 24h format (default 23)
# IDLE_PING_SILENT_START=23

# Silent window end hour (default 8)
# IDLE_PING_SILENT_END=8

# Timezone (default Asia/Hong_Kong)
# IDLE_PING_TZ=Asia/Hong_Kong

# ===== Pause mechanism =====
# How many unanswered shipments before the dice auto-pauses (default 2)
# IDLE_PING_PAUSE_AFTER=2

# Pause-notice style pool, comma-separated (default: 4 built-in styles)
# IDLE_PING_PAUSE_STYLES=月光詩意,貼心關心,幽默玩味,自嘲

# ===== Production monitoring (heartbeat) =====
# Local heartbeat file — updated by heartbeat.sh on every run;
# watchdog.sh alerts if it goes stale (cron silently died).
# IDLE_PING_HEARTBEAT_FILE=$HOME/.openclaw/workspace/curiosity/heartbeat.txt

# Optional external monitoring ping (Healthchecks.io / Cronitor / any GET-ping URL).
# Set this to get email/Telegram alerts when the cron stops.
# e.g. https://hc-ping.com/your-uuid-here
# IDLE_PING_HEARTBEAT_URL=

# Heartbeat staleness threshold in minutes (watchdog alert trigger; default 60)
# IDLE_PING_WATCHDOG_STALE_MIN=60

# Heartbeat / watchdog cron intervals (install-time; re-run install.sh to apply)
# IDLE_PING_HEARTBEAT_EVERY=10m
# IDLE_PING_WATCHDOG_EVERY=1h
